{"article_ids": ["9f86890e896c66b0"], "canonical_title": "Is Human-Readable Text Necessary for Effective LLM Fine-Tuning?", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.8, "description": "A new arXiv paper introduces Desired‑Update‑Aligned Synthetic Data (DASA), a technique that creates continuous synthetic input embeddings guided by activation‑gradient feedback from a frozen reference model. The method tests whether model‑conditioned training representations can retain or improve fine‑tuning utility without requiring human‑readable textual data.", "entities": ["term:dasa"], "first_seen": "2026-09-30T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_9f86890e896c66b0", "importance_score": 6.69, "last_updated": "2026-09-30T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["d6b9f5e651b1891e", "05f4f9748885e1c5"], "canonical_title": "Introducing GPT-6.1 Sol", "category": "model_release", "confidence": 0.95, "description": "OpenAI announced GPT‑6.1 Sol, a model offering near‑Astra level reasoning for coding, computer use and professional work at about one‑fifth the token price of Astra’s standard API. AWS confirmed the model is generally available on Amazon Bedrock, extending its access to developers.", "entities": ["model:gpt", "model:gpt-6.1", "org:amazon", "term:gpt"], "first_seen": "2026-09-29T10:00:00Z", "id": "evt_d6b9f5e651b1891e", "importance_score": 6.25, "last_updated": "2026-09-29T19:34:14Z", "source_ids": ["openai", "aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["6071f63e21f64254", "3e2da47f73a8838a", "2fd483a5ede3dbd8"], "canonical_title": "DevDay 2026 Recap", "category": "other", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "At DevDay 2026 OpenAI announced GPT‑6.1 Sol, a new language model that delivers significant improvements over GPT‑6 Sol and is described as nearly matching the capabilities of GPT‑6 Astra while costing about 20% of the price. The model is targeted at complex professional tasks such as code writing, debugging, document understanding, and multi‑step business workflows.", "entities": ["model:gpt", "model:gpt-6", "model:gpt-6.1", "org:openai", "product:chatgpt", "term:gpt"], "first_seen": "2026-09-29T10:00:00Z", "id": "evt_6071f63e21f64254", "importance_score": 6.24, "last_updated": "2026-09-29T18:27:48Z", "source_ids": ["openai", "techcrunch-ai", "simon-willison"]}
{"article_ids": ["76c15d3fb8416cf2"], "canonical_title": "Beyond Symmetric Agents: Cognitive Diversity and Multi-Agent Debate in Small Language Models", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.78, "description": "Researchers evaluated multi-agent debate (MAD) using 23 small open-weight language models from eleven vendors across five tasks, running over 5,500 debate and control experiments. They compared symmetric (identical) agents to heterogeneous agents and found that cognitive diversity among agents—differences in model architecture, training data, or vendor—led to measurable improvements in reasoning accuracy and factuality over single-model inference.", "entities": ["term:mad"], "first_seen": "2026-09-30T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_76c15d3fb8416cf2", "importance_score": 6.14, "last_updated": "2026-09-30T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
